== page api.md -> data/out/api.html (1140 bytes, 4 headings)
<!doctype html>
<title>API reference</title>
<nav>
<ul>
<li><a href="#toc_1">API reference
</a>
<ul>
<li><a href="#toc_2">Build
</a></li>
<li><a href="#toc_3">Serve
</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</nav>
<main>
<h1 id="toc_1">API reference</h1>
<details class="toc" open>
<summary>Table of Contents</summary>
<ul>
<li><a href="#toc_2">Build
</a>
<ul>
<li><a href="#toc_3">Arguments</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="#toc_4">Serve
</a></li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="toc_2">Build</h2>
<p><code>build(src, out, *, theme=None)</code> renders every page under <code>src</code>.</p>
<h3 id="toc_3">Arguments</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>src</strong>: the source folder</li>
<li><strong>out</strong>: the output folder</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="toc_3">Serve</h2>
<p><code>serve(out, port=8000)</code> serves <code>out</code> over <abbr title="Hypertext Transfer Protocol">HTTP</abbr>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note</strong>: the server is for previews only.
Use a real web server in production.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Math: <span class="math">\(O(n \log n)\)</span> for <em>n</em> pages, with the bound</p>
<div class="math">$$
T(n) = 2T(n/2) + n
$$</div>
</main>
